  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is RNA-only multiprofile with scvi_n200 and avgpool (config_005: 0.6501 acc, 0.6275 F1), while image-only models remain weak (about 0.21-0.33 acc). The key unresolved question is whether adding image features to the best RNA setting provides any complementary signal. config_030 tests this by extending config_005 with a tested image encoder (resnet50) and the simplest fusion baseline (concat), while keeping the RNA encoder, profile setting, and aggregation fixed at their best-performing values. This is the most informative next experiment because it directly evaluates the value of multimodality under the current best representation; if it improves, it justifies further fusion/image-encoder exploration, and if it does not, it discourages spending budget on more complex multimodal variants."
}

